{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The harder and more useful variant. The problem does not give you a width — it gives you a **rule**, and asks for the longest or shortest window that satisfies it."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The two-phase loop"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The right edge always advances, growing the window. The left edge only advances when the rule has been violated, shrinking until it holds again."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "src": "/drawings/2f40ab8a-978a-4132-8622-2375d299b771.svg",
      "alt": "A window whose right edge expands and whose left edge contracts when a rule is broken",
      "caption": "Grow from the right until the rule breaks, then shrink from the left until it holds",
      "width": 900,
      "height": 280,
      "scene": {
